The export is dated 4 October. The live course page, checked 29 October, says ticket #4471 closed on 5 October: the parser is fixed; the hint is won't fix because booking-v3 was retired.

## What the desk table shows

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table deduplicates report IDs and groups by tenant locale and form, using the original components. Intake tags and matching subjects do not establish the cause.

## Separate problems

### Shared parser

Day-first tenants reach a parser that reads month first. R-41200 describes 7 April becoming 4 July. The engineering update says: fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales.

### booking-v3 hint

The form prints MM/DD/YYYY for day-first tenants, while the form interprets the tenant's date order. R-41230 describes 6 January becoming 1 June. Engineering declined this fix because booking-v3 was retired.

### Remaining investigation

The table footnote identifies reports read as one-day moves. R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 describe day shifts, cross-timezone disagreement, or an invite arriving before booking creation. They remain included in the parser table count; they are not additional reports. Their cause is unverified, and the engineering update does not explicitly resolve these symptoms.

## Tickets

- [Parser: 379 reports](https://github.com/jwilk123/mega-s01e03-replay/issues/1). Engineering reports the parser fixed.
- [Hint: 33 reports](https://github.com/jwilk123/mega-s01e03-replay/issues/2). Engineering declined the fix after booking-v3 retirement.
- [Investigation: 5 overlapping reports](https://github.com/jwilk123/mega-s01e03-replay/issues/3). Cause remains unverified; these are already counted under parser.

## Triage recommendation

Group reports only when reproduction and tenant context support the same cause. Preserve the accepted decision record 0001; propose a new superseding record rather than changing its history. Recheck the live desk update before any claim.

